## Summary

The lookout by Goblin Village's south gate has a ladder in three locs: `goblin_ladder_bottom` (Climb-up, level 0), `goblin_ladder_middle` (no ops) and `goblin_ladder_top` (Climb-down, level 2). None of them has a content group in `.data/raw-cache/server/loc/loc.toml`, so the generic ladder scripts don't bind them, and `GoblinCaveLadders` (#328) only covers the cave ladders: Climb-up does nothing. A generic one-level ladder wouldn't fit anyway, since the top is on level 2.

`GoblinCaveLadders` now binds the two: Climb-up and Climb-down play `human_reachforladder` and move the player between level 0 and level 2 on the same tile, like the cave ladders' climb.

This was part of #367 (Goblin Diplomacy, whose third armour crate is on the lookout); it is split out as its own fix. Neither PR depends on the other.

